    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Regarding the kitchen staff—should I provide a printed sheet for every station, or is it better to have a single master list that's checked off as dishes are completed? Also, for the buffet, do you have any tips for managing the flow of people so they don't accidentally use the same tongs for different dishes and cause issues?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the kitchen staff, I strongly recommend a printed, station-specific sheet for every chef, rather than a single master list. A master list is too easily lost or misinterpreted in the chaos, and a dedicated sheet ensures the person plating the vegan option knows exactly what needs to go into that specific dish. To manage the flow at the buffet, you need to implement dedicated serving utensils for *every single dish*, and perhaps even designate separate, clearly marked serving stations for high-risk items like those containing nuts. This prevents the dreaded \"tongs-crossing\" scenario, which is a major hazard.",
